    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\binom{a+b}{a}(a-1)!(b-1)!$ ways.",
      "worked": "Choose $a$ people for the first table; the remaining $b$ sit at the second. Their circular-arrangement counts are $(a-1)!$ and $(b-1)!$. The tables are distinct, so no division for interchanging tables is needed.\n\n$$N=\\binom{a+b}{a}(a-1)!(b-1)!.$$",
